{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01127",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.64,
      "end_seconds": 5.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.11,
      "text": "doctor, we're ready in room two, I've already taken the observations"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.01,
      "end_seconds": 14.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.81,
      "end_seconds": 23.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "Honestly it's lower back pain and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.75,
      "end_seconds": 26.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "did it come on recently?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.87,
      "end_seconds": 34.02,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "Around two months... no wait, it's more like about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.6,
      "end_seconds": 44.94,
      "duration_seconds": 9.34,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.53,
      "end_seconds": 51.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "I'd give it a three out of ten i notice it more with bending"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.02,
      "end_seconds": 56.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "any stiffness in the morning as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.7,
      "end_seconds": 75.73,
      "duration_seconds": 18.03,
      "text": "Yeah that too. And And tingling in my left foot too. As for tingling in my left foot it happens on and off. I've also had pain going down the back of my left leg for about three months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.8,
      "end_seconds": 78.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "how about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.07,
      "end_seconds": 81.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "I've never touched a cigarette"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.5,
      "end_seconds": 84.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "And And alcohol how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.45,
      "end_seconds": 88.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.54,
      "end_seconds": 92.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "what line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.93,
      "end_seconds": 98.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.75,
      "end_seconds": 101.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.97,
      "end_seconds": 105.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "My partner and our baby"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.12,
      "end_seconds": 108.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.23,
      "end_seconds": 114.77,
      "duration_seconds": 5.54,
      "text": "Metoprolol. I take it 50 milligrams, twice a day for my pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 119.63,
      "end_seconds": 124.96,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 100 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 125.55,
      "end_seconds": 129.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Hm. Do you have the latest prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.82,
      "end_seconds": 143.06,
      "duration_seconds": 12.24,
      "text": "No I left it at home. I take hydrocortisone cream when needed for the eczema. I'm on escitalopram 10 milligrams maybe once a day for the anxiety."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.74,
      "end_seconds": 147.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.1,
      "text": "do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.2,
      "end_seconds": 156.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "no, you know, it's at home. Paracetamol, when needed"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.61,
      "end_seconds": 160.07,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "And what strength is that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.77,
      "end_seconds": 163.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "it's 1 gram"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.51,
      "end_seconds": 187.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.56,
      "text": "so, any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.53,
      "end_seconds": 191.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.17,
      "text": "no I'm not allergic to anything"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.85,
      "end_seconds": 203.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.27,
      "text": "So, did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.77,
      "end_seconds": 209.67,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "Yes I had a bunion operation six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.69,
      "end_seconds": 213.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 215.1,
      "end_seconds": 220.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "High blood pressure, for two years. I've had eczema, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.02,
      "end_seconds": 222.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "is there anything more?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.48,
      "end_seconds": 226.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Anxiety, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.42,
      "end_seconds": 239.82,
      "duration_seconds": 11.4,
      "text": "Yes anxiety is known to us good to have that clear. Let me check a few things. Any bowel problems weakness in the foot or bladder problems?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.97,
      "end_seconds": 243.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "no, nothing to report there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.49,
      "end_seconds": 251.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Any fever, numbness between the legs or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.76,
      "end_seconds": 257.62,
      "duration_seconds": 5.86,
      "text": "no fever numbness between the legs or weight loss none of it"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.36,
      "end_seconds": 261.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.69,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.83,
      "end_seconds": 264.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "No, all normal there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 267.28,
      "end_seconds": 277.39,
      "duration_seconds": 10.11,
      "text": "here are the numbers, doctor temperature is 36.4 degrees, pulse is 76 beats a minute, oxygen saturation is 98 percent, pressure 119 over 76."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.31,
      "end_seconds": 279.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "good, thank you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.98,
      "end_seconds": 311.15,
      "duration_seconds": 22.17,
      "text": "so based on your history this is probably sciatica from a lumbar disc irritation. That's my thinking for now and it may change as we learn more. A muscle strain is also on my list. I'll request an MRI of the lower back it'll help with sciatica. I think blood tests makes sense here for back pain"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.16,
      "end_seconds": 339.21,
      "duration_seconds": 27.05,
      "text": "Let's use naproxen, 500 milligrams, twice a day with food, for one week. You take it by mouth. That should help with back and leg pain. Stay active and keep walking, bed rest makes this slower to settle. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 340.76,
      "end_seconds": 342.1,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "I I understand."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.2,
      "end_seconds": 354.36,
      "duration_seconds": 11.16,
      "text": "Do get help quickly if you get numbness between the legs or trouble passing urine. Let's plan a check in four weeks. Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.58,
      "end_seconds": 363.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "Right I'll do that. Thank you doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.16,
      "end_seconds": 365.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}